$DATUM 8-(4-Azido-2,3,5,6-pentafluorophenyl)-4,4-difluoro-4-bora-3a,4a-diaza-s-indacene
(7).
8-(2,3,4,5,6-Pentafluorophenyl)-4,4-difluoro-4-bora-3a,4a-diaza-s-indacene
6 (100 mg, 0.28 mmol) was dissolved under argon atmosphere in dry DMF
(4.0 mL), sodium azide (21.8 mg, 0.34 mmol) was added and the reaction
mixture stirred for 30 min. at 50 °C. After aqueous workup, extraction
with DCM and drying over sodium sulfate, the crude product was evaporated
to dryness and purified by column chromatography (DCM/n-hexane = 3:1).
Azide-BODIPY 7 as red-golden solid (102 mg, 0.26 mmol, 96%). 1H-NMR (700
MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.52-6.61 (m, 2H, 3,7-HPyrrole), 6.79-6.86 (m, 2H,
2,8-HPyrrole), 7.93-8.01 (m, 2H, 1,9-HPyrrole) ppm. 13C-NMR (176 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 119.79 (3,7-CPyrrole), 130.59 (2,8-CPyrrole), 134.97 (5-C
meso ), 146.53 (1,9-CPyrrole) ppm. 19F-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -137.06
(dd, J = 19.8, 8.0 Hz, 2F, Ar-F ortho ), -144.82 (dd, J = 56.6, 28.3 Hz,
2F, BF2), -149.64 (dd, J = 20.4, 8.8 Hz, 2F, Ar-F meta ) ppm. IR
(Substance): ν = 2127.1 (N3) cm-1. HRMS (ESI-TOF): m/z calc. for
C15H6BF6N5Na [M + Na]+: 404.0513; found: 404.0487. UV-VIS (DCM), λ max
[log ε (L · mol-1 · cm-1mol-1 · cm-1)]: 355 (4.19), 519 (4.85) nm.
Fluorescence emission (acetone): λ max = 561 nm at λ Excitation = 520 nm.
